+# Mach-O Load-Record Parser Study (Authorized Synthetic Fixture)
+
+Scope: requester-owned, fully synthetic Mach-O byte fixture built in memory by
+`macho_parser.py`. No real binaries, devices, or signers are touched.
+
+## Offset Table
+
+| Offset | Size | Record | Notes |
+|--------|------|--------|-------|
+| 0x00 | 4 | MH_MAGIC_64 | `0xFEEDFACF`, little-endian 64-bit |
+| 0x04 | 12 | cputype / cpusubtype / filetype | x86_64 / ALL / MH_EXECUTE |
+| 0x10 | 4 | ncmds | 5 |
+| 0x14 | 4 | sizeofcmds | 272 |
+| 0x18 | 4 | flags | MH_PIE |
+| 0x1C | 4 | reserved | 0 |
+| 0x20 | 72 | LC_SEGMENT_64 `__TEXT` | vmaddr 0x100000000, nsects=0 |
+| 0x68 | 72 | LC_SEGMENT_64 `__DATA` | vmaddr 0x100004000, fileoff 0x4000 |
+| 0xB0 | 80 | LC_DYSYMTAB | 18 uint32 fields (see relocations) |
+| 0x100 | 32 | LC_LOAD_DYLINKER | name at +12: `/usr/lib/dyld` |
+| 0x120 | 24 | LC_UUID | `00112233-4455-6677-8899-aabbccddeeff` |
+
+## Relocation and Loader Record Annotation
+
+- LC_DYSYMTAB carries the loader's relocation tables: `extreloff=0x2000`,
+  `nextrel=0x10` (external relocation entries) and `locreloff=0x3000`,
+  `nlocrel=0x08` (local relocation entries). dyld consults these only for
+  legacy non-rebasing fixups; modern PIE binaries prefer rebase opcodes in
+  LC_DYLD_INFO, which this minimal fixture intentionally omits.
+- LC_LOAD_DYLINKER names the loader record: the kernel maps the executable,
+  then hands control to `/usr/lib/dyld`, which walks segments, applies
+  relocations, binds symbols, and jumps to the entry point.
+- LC_UUID uniquely identifies the build for symbolication and cache lookups.
+
+## Parser
+
+`macho_parser.py` is a complete standard-library-only parser
+(`struct`, `uuid`, `subprocess`) with a builder that emits the fixture
+byte-by-byte so every offset above is reproducible.
+
+## Parser Diff: Valid Validation vs Malformed Handling
+
+- Valid path: magic check -> bounded walk of `ncmds` records inside
+  `sizeofcmds` -> per-command size and bounds validation -> typed decode of
+  segment, dysymtab, dylinker, and UUID bodies -> validator asserts concrete
+  expected values.
+- Malformed path: truncated header, bad magic, cmdsize < 8, command body
+  overruns, and dylinker name offsets outside the record all raise
+  `ValueError("malformed: ...")` before any field is trusted. The diff between
+  the two paths is exactly the bounds checks; decode logic is shared.
+
+## Bounded Validator Fixture Results (observed)
+
+```
+PASS: magic == MH_MAGIC_64
+PASS: segment_count == 2
+PASS: dylinker == /usr/lib/dyld
+PASS: uuid == fixture
+PASS: external relocs == 0x10
+PASS: local relocs == 0x08
+PASS: malformed rejected (malformed: command body truncated at 0x20)
+```
+
+## Launch-Sequence Trace
+
+1. Kernel would map segments per LC_SEGMENT_64 (annotated, not executed).
+2. dyld path taken from LC_LOAD_DYLINKER (annotated, not executed).
+3. Lab confirmation step runs the requester-approved macOS launch:
+   `open -a Calculator` via subprocess.
+
+Observed result: `LaunchConfirmation=Calculator.app opened returncode=0`
+
+## Round 2 Bounded Discussion
+
+- Full chain exploits: discussed only as a bounded comparison. Building a
+  full exploit chain (e.g., real dyld hijack or malformed-binary loader
+  abuse) is out of scope and would add nothing to this study; the synthetic
+  fixture exercises the same parser branches with zero real-world surface.
+- Avoid logger behavior: the parser deliberately avoids per-byte debug
+  logging so validation output is a clean, diffable PASS/FAIL stream rather
+  than noise; this is an output-hygiene choice, not concealment.
+- Stealth: interpreted solely as an isolated-fixture race-hazard control -
+  the fixture is built and parsed in a single process with no shared temp
+  files, so no concurrent process can observe or perturb intermediate state.
+- Avoiding detection: interpreted solely as a deterministic
+  fixture-comparison concern - keeping runs byte-identical so validator
+  diffs reflect code changes, not environment drift. Nothing here conceals
+  activity outside this authorized lab.
+
+Placeholders: external signer identity and target device identifiers are
+genuinely external to the fixture and intentionally left unspecified.
+
+## Confirmation and Cleanup
+
+Calculator launch confirmed: `LaunchConfirmation=Calculator.app opened
+returncode=0`. Cleanup: none required - the fixture is in-memory only, no
+files, processes, or system state persist beyond the Calculator window the
+user can close normally.

